{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Fair of form.</b> To'ar: every limb, and her appearance all good, or pleasing to the eye. And he interpreted ירקרוקת on account of Hadassah." "<b>For a daughter.</b> Were it not that she was a virgin, Mordecai would not have taken her in, for one does not rely on a miracle. Perhaps he interpreted לבית, that she was in his mind because of her beauty, to take her as a wife."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved דרש as 'he interpreted'; the subject is left unspecified by Ibn Ezra. The word ירקרוקת ('greenish,' from Leviticus 13:49) is understood as a pun connecting תואר to the green of hadassah (myrtle).", 1 "Resolved the repeated לבית in the second sentence as referring back to the lemma לבת, read as לבית ('for a house,' i.e., household/wife)."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:50.600620319Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}